{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "policy": "Every upstream DiamaneOS builds from. forks: repositories we fork and patch (the forks the DiamaneOS manifest selects on android17, and the common kernel); the fork branch is the pin and upstream is the reference it follows. sources: pinned upstream inputs that are not forked, including the upstream projects imported into kernel_qcom-6.1, whose import record is config/kernel-upstream-fp6.json; pin names the file and field that hold the pinned value. newer (newer_branches, newer_tags for sources): branches or tags that would supersede the followed reference, ordered by their capture group; a source measures newer_tags from the release its pin records (release_field). Fairphone forks and imports track the public-build branch where it exists, otherwise rc; CodeLinaro forks and imports track a release tag, or the newest release branch that contains the pinned commit with its release tags as newer. Checks read remote refs only and never move a branch or push; fork updates are rebased into a local candidate branch for build and review, kernel imports are new commits on the upstream branch of kernel_qcom-6.1 merged into android17, and adopting either is a reviewed, signed change.",
